1. What this is
   This repository holds the source of Komiks·Lab: program code, comic scripts,
   drawings generated in code, dictionaries, word lists, grammar material and the
   texts of the interface. Everything here is the property of BILOHASH.

2. What you may do
   You may read this repository, study how it is built, run it locally on your own
   machine for personal learning, and quote short excerpts with a visible credit to
   https://bilohash.com/comiks/.
   Teachers and learners may use the live site at https://bilohash.com/comiks/ in
   class and at home, free of charge, under the terms shown on that site.

3. What you may not do without written permission
   - copy, publish or host this project, in whole or in substantial part, anywhere else;
   - sell it, include it in a paid product or service, or use it commercially;
   - distribute modified versions, or present it as your own work;
   - reuse the comics, drawings, dictionaries, word lists or recorded voices
     as separate material, including as training data.

4. Permission
   Written permission can be requested at https://bilohash.com/comiks/ through the
   feedback form. Permission is given in writing and only for what it names.

5. The server part
   The server API (accounts, community walls, feedback, AI calls, writing feedback,
